<title>SPAIN: Argentaria to advise Aldeasa in sale.</title>
<headline>Argentaria to advise Aldeasa in sale.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Argentaria has been elected adviser in the privatisation of Spanish duty-free shop manager Aldeasa, the bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Aldeasa is expected to be privatised later this year, the bank said.</p>
<p>The government controls 80 percent of Aldeasa while state-owned airport authority AENA owns 20 percent.</p>
<p>Aldeasa posted a gross profit of some eight billion pesetas and a turnover of some 50 billion pesetas in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
</text>
